WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.460
Hey guys, it's Jan here!

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.979
The latest movie I've caught on the big screen
is Disney's newest animated feature, Zootropolis,

00:00:06.979 --> 00:00:10.250
which, depending what country you're in, is
also called Zootopia!

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.540
The film follows what happens when a scam-artist
fox and a hard-working rabbit who's a rookie

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.140
cop join together to crack a mysterious case
of missing mammals.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.040
Basically, it's a mix of buddy cop movie,
odd-couple comedy, and classic whodunit with

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.190
shades of film noirs like Chinatown.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:29.160
The voice cast is superb and features the
likes of Luther's Idris Elba as cape buffalo

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.730
cop Chief Bogo and Whiplash's JK Simmons as
Mayor Lionheart.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:38.030
And I love the teaming up of Once Upon A Time
star Ginnifer Goodwin as the optimistic rabbit,

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:42.949
Judy Hopps, and Arrested Development's Jason
Bateman as the laid-back hustling fox, Nick

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:43.949
Wilde.

00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:47.120
They play really nicely off each other and
make a superb comic duo.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.190
Pop star Shakira also gets a cameo as a pop
star called Gazelle, and performs a new upbeat

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:57.170
and super-earwormy song called Try Everything,
written by Sia and Stargate.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:01.269
Speaking of music, the film's score was composed
by Michael Giacchino, and as you'd expect

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:05.970
it perfectly fits the movie's tone throughout,
right down to its Hitchcock and The Godfather-inspired

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:06.970
moments.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.770
In case you're interested, it's actually Giacchino's
first score for a feature-length animated

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:14.930
Disney movie, though, of course, he's done
plenty of brilliant work for Pixar including

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.420
Inside Out, The Incredibles, and Up.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.440
Directors Byron Howard, who gave us Tangled,
Rich Moore, who gave us Wreck-It Ralph, and

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:25.280
Jared Bush, who's directing for the first
time and also co-wrote the script with Wreck-It

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.180
Ralph writer Phil Johnston, have done a great
job bringing to life the beautifully detailed

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.680
city of Zootropolis.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.500
And Disney's animators deserve handfuls of
high fives all round for creating such a beautifully

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:40.780
colourful and incredibly well-thought-out
world which is cleverly divided into different

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.940
districts based on climates and species.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:47.980
For example, there's Sahara Square for desert
animals, Tundratown for polar bears and moose,

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:53.020
and for rodents Little Rodentia, which is
the location of an ingenious chase scene.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.290
The story itself feels particularly apt and
well-timed, dealing as it does with prejudice

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:01.820
and inclusivity, using different species and
specifically the idea of predators and prey

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:06.479
as an interesting way into those issues, playing
both with and against people's preconceived

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:11.069
notions of different animals, from shrews
to sloths, and elephants to cheetahs.

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:16.130
The film mainly manages to avoid being preachy
and only feels a touch on the nose at times.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:20.450
The movie is full of knowing humour, including
jokes about Disney's own movies, and you'll

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:25.689
also see and hear tons of pop culture references
and some brilliantly funny easter eggs to

00:02:25.689 --> 00:02:27.340
well-known films and TV shows.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:31.510
In fact, I've made a video with all those
easter eggs and references, and I'll put the

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.329
link here as soon as it's live!

00:02:33.329 --> 00:02:38.549
So, to sum up, Zootropolis is a charming odd-couple
comedy which blends a gorgeously realised

00:02:38.549 --> 00:02:43.639
world, superb voice cast, timely message,
and elements from classic films and pop culture

00:02:43.639 --> 00:02:46.920
to create a movie that has plenty to keep
both adults and kids entertained.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.519
At around 1 hour 50 minutes, the movie feels
a touch on the long side, but I did still

00:02:51.519 --> 00:02:54.609
very much enjoy my time visiting the city
of Zootropolis.

00:02:54.609 --> 00:02:57.120
Zootropolis gets 4 out of 5 Flicks.

